we've selected five maps to give you a  small taste of the range of denial ops  awaiting in multiplayer  later today you'll see them playing but  here's a few of my teammates to share  what they love  most from how they were made  my name is brittany vitelman i'm a level  designer i'm kendall snow  associate level designer i'm brittany  perello producer  i'm matt cutrus senior level designer in  satellite a top secret american recon  satellite has lost  power and crashed in the deserts of  angola  with higher dgi forces closing in now  it's a race to secure the crash site  what i love about satellite is the fact  that it's just this amazing natural  space  because larger maps have more components  we can apply more details into maps like  satellite  which make them feel even more natural  the satellite at the center is like a  king of the hill  anyone who wants it has to run toward  you because it's raised higher than the  rest of the map  i'm usually playing one of two ways all  in full ham  dying again and again or in objective  modes i'll flank and get the jump on  people  satellite scratches both of those edges  even though it's an outdoor space the  map's two different regions mean i can  play long  and short range tactics i'll be honest  i am trash with a sniper rifle but a  shotgun  that i can do i have always been a big  fan of close quarters combat  and there is great cat and mouse style  gameplay in satellite  the crash satellite is a super fun spot  to try and outplay radios  predict which way they'll circle the  debris to run up behind them or just  duck inside the satellite and take their  shot  this is going to be one of those classic  black ops maps the world knows and loves  for how quickly engagements fire up  east and west collide on the open seas  in a top secret mission  inspired by a real-life event project  azorian cia  jsoc and soviet forces converged to  recover a sunken prototype nuclear  soviet submarine from the ocean floor  calm waters of armada explode into  massive naval conflict as players battle  for control of large naval vessels with  no  lanes walling you in players can engage  on ships decks  in the water and on vehicles like wake  runners and gunboats  armada is chaos in the best way  this really cool map that gives this  amazing sense of exploration there are  so many little individual areas to find  and new ways to surround or flank your  enemies and get the upper hand  a hidden safe house has been discovered  right in the heart of the ussr  in the shadow of moscow's opulent train  station  with sped snaps dispatched the area has  gone hot  so the moscow map is set in the dead  heart of a big city  so you're wandering through these  streets with a bunch of cars and there's  tall buildings on either side of you  there's this sense that you've been  dropped into a point in history  first thing i do is run right to the  center because that's where  all lanes cross in the moscow map  and eventually it doesn't take long  people are gonna run through  the metro station so you can just sit  there and wait but chances are there's  gonna be people running right into your  line of fire right off the bat  it's a classic three-lane map where  teamwork really makes the dream work  january 17 1984 this location  is heavily influenced by miami's famous  or perhaps infamous  ocean drive this is a night map but one  unlike players have seen before you can  sneak through dark shadowy alleys  go out onto the beach out into the ocean  you can dive in the water  and wait along the coast to get the drop  on the other side  or you can just go right down the street  and bask in the neon light  the first time i played through miami i  could hear this 80s nightclub music  playing through the walls of one of the  buildings  little details make it lifelike and it  becomes this  joy to experience  basically my goal is to never be on the  main street in the center because that  is  sniper heaven and that is britney hell  so i always go and try to flank and get  those snipers from the back  our art and design teams worked really  hard to bring the best  possible night experience to the players  you'll see that play out when you sneak  in the shadows on the beach  or engage enemies in the center strip it  really makes people feel  like they're in miami in the 80s it's  pretty  pretty cool  in crossroads nato has learned a large  soviet missile convoy is on its way to  the border special forces dispatch  alongside mi6  to ambush the convoy and secure the  weapons before all hell breaks loose  it's one of our most cinematic maps with  a boots on the ground field that feels  pulled from the campaign your team will  want to hold down and protect its own  outposts to guarantee access to one of  these tanks  but infantry combat doesn't take a back  seat and crossroads as natural terrain  and foliage  masks movements and provides tactical  advantages there's a bunch of  snowmobiles when you first spawn and  it's a mad dash to grab one  and now running people over with the  snowmobile is my favorite thing to do  each environment changes the dynamic of  how you play  and caters to unique loadouts crossroads  is a bigger map and that allows you to  play  the way you want to play  the beaches of miami a frozen over lake  the open ocean our visual research  department  racked up miles visiting them all  because if you're going to deploy around  the globe in this game  that required them to do the same the  mission for  our artist is absolute authenticity step  one in that process is photo scanning  thousands of real world objects  terrains and materials those assets  ensure our  upgraded physically based renderer  delivers the best looking black ops yet  true 4k high dynamic range with the true  color and tone  ray tracing on systems that support it  photometric lighting courtesy of our  luminaire  system and overhauled contour terrain  system the result is gritty  it's believable i dare say 